[{"_1":2},"llms/mdx",{"_3":4},"data","# Lamassu Updates (/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/overview)\n\n\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Lamassu Updates (also called the OTA Update Service) orchestrates over-the-air software updates for IoT fleets. You publish an update, choose which devices receive it, and watch the rollout. The service builds the package that [SWUpdate](https://swupdate.org/) clients install, and can sign and encrypt it.\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  There is one HTTP API and two interchangeable backends behind it, chosen with the `mode` setting. The backend decides which update server the devices talk to, so the systems around the service depend on it.\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  What it connects to [#what-it-connects-to]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  | System                                              | What it does                                                                                                                                    | `native`      | `hawkbit`                                                                                 |\n  | --------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n  | [Lamassu IoT](/docs/platform/iot-fleets/overview)   | Device registry (device groups) and KMS. Signing keys live in its KMS                                                                           | Required      | Optional: without it, groups are read from the `group:<id>` tags on hawkBit's own targets |\n  | [WFX](https://github.com/siemens/wfx)               | Job orchestration. Each device update is a WFX job that the device polls                                                                        | Required      | Not used                                                                                  |\n  | [Eclipse hawkBit](https://www.eclipse.org/hawkbit/) | Update server. Stores packs, modules and rollouts, and devices poll it                                                                          | Not used      | Required                                                                                  |\n  | Postgres                                            | The service's own data                                                                                                                          | Required      | Required                                                                                  |\n  | swugenerator                                        | Python tool, bundled in the [ota repository](https://github.com/lamassuiot/ota), that assembles the signed and optionally encrypted `.swu` file | When building | When building                                                                             |\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  The Lamassu dashboard is the web interface for this API. It reads its base URL from `LAMASSU_UPDATES_API` in `public/config.js` (when unset it falls back to the main API base URL) and appends `/updates/v1` and `/symkms/v1` itself. It also reads `GET /updates/v1/capabilities` once and hides the features the active backend does not support.\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Choose your backend [#choose-your-backend]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  The HTTP API is the same either way. What differs is who stores the data and who the devices talk to.\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  |                              | `native` (default)                                       | `hawkbit`                                                               |\n  | ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n  | Stores packs, launches, jobs | This service's Postgres, plus WFX                        | An Eclipse hawkBit server                                               |\n  | Devices poll                 | WFX                                                      | hawkBit (DDI API)                                                       |\n  | A pack is built              | As a whole, from all its modules' files, into one `.swu` | One `.swu` (or raw deliverable) per module, built in the module catalog |\n  | Per-device encryption        | Supported                                                | Not supported                                                           |\n  | Pick it when                 | You start from scratch, or need per-device encryption    | hawkBit is already your fleet's update backend                          |\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Set it with the `mode` field of the [configuration](/docs/platform/updates/reference/configuration). The backends are not equivalent in every feature: see [Capabilities](/docs/platform/updates/reference/capabilities) and [hawkBit mode](/docs/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode).\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Where to go next [#where-to-go-next]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  | I want to...                                | Read                                                                                                         |\n  | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n  | Run the whole stack locally                 | [Getting started](/docs/platform/updates/getting-started)                                                    |\n  | Understand the terms (pack, module, launch) | [Concepts](/docs/platform/updates/concepts) and [Data model](/docs/platform/updates/data-model)              |\n  | See the components and how data flows       | [Architecture](/docs/platform/updates/architecture) and [Flows](/docs/platform/updates/flows)                |\n  | Publish an update and roll it out           | [Publish and roll out an update](/docs/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out)                         |\n  | Try the whole flow with curl                | [Native](/docs/platform/updates/guides/native-curl) or [hawkBit](/docs/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl) |\n  | Do it from the web interface                | [Use the dashboard](/docs/platform/updates/guides/dashboard)                                                 |\n  | Connect a device                            | [Connect a device](/docs/platform/updates/guides/connect-a-device)                                           |\n  | Use an existing hawkBit                     | [hawkBit mode](/docs/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode)                                                          |\n  | Sign or encrypt updates                     | [Signing and encryption](/docs/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption)                                      |\n  | Set a config field                          | [Configuration](/docs/platform/updates/reference/configuration)                                              |\n  | Call the API                                | [API reference](/docs/platform/updates/reference/api)                                                        |\n  | Deploy, scale, back up or upgrade it        | [Operations](/docs/platform/updates/operations)                                                              |\n  | Secure it                                   | [Security](/docs/platform/updates/security)                                                                  |\n  | Fix a problem                               | [Troubleshooting](/docs/platform/updates/troubleshooting)                                                    |\n  | See what is not supported                   | [Limitations](/docs/platform/updates/limitations)                                                            |\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  The source code, sample configurations and Helm chart are in the [ota repository](https://github.com/lamassuiot/ota).\n</div>\n"]
